    {
      "id": "claim_c22ef9beb673411582590e83c59ec59f",
      "statement": "Ask Sangam's SQL tool runs as the caller, not the owner: ask_access sets the agent_caller context variable from the principal per /agent request, and the SQL executor applies set_caller inside a read-only transaction, defaulting to anon when no caller is set; Import keeps the owner because it writes the catalog. So grants and RLS on a new table govern what catalogued queries return.",
      "evidence": [
